# 0.8 UNRELEASED

-   Require Python 3.12 or newer and PyGlossary 5.4.2 or newer.
-   Improve virtual environment creation and configuration registration,
    including actionable ICU dependency errors.
-   dicts.mk: Make StarDict builds safe under parallel Make execution, rebuild
    missing outputs, and preserve existing outputs when conversion fails.
-   dicts.mk: Preserve StarDict synonyms in release archives and installations.
    Honor unsupported formats and retain the archive layout with custom
    build directories.
-   Install and uninstall all supported binary dictionary formats.
-   Preserve semantic version suffixes, correctly order FreeDict revisions,
    and align API schema validation with supported dictionary versions.
    Select tools releases by semantic version and use the selected tag's date.
-   Validate the configured API output, propagate generation failures,
    and clean up remote access after failures. Support Jing through
    `USE_JING=1`, with xmllint remaining the default validator.
-   Add forced WikDict downloads and preserve existing dictionaries when
    replacement fails.
-   Run Unison synchronization noninteractively and preserve the caller's
    environment when remote access fails.
-   Update the Esperanto-English importer for the October 2024 source,
    including UTF-8 byte order mark handling and corrected metadata.
-   Add `make test` and parallel component runners through `make -j4 test`,
    with support for selecting the Python interpreter.

# 0.7

-   Replace the legacy StarDict converter with PyGlossary and produce
    compressed release archives with checksums.
-   Include StarDict downloads in the generated dictionary API.
-   Support deploying individual dictionary formats, including adding a
    format to an existing release.
-   Use tools release archive URLs with predictable extracted directory
    names for packaging.
-   Update the WikDict download source and prepend import changelog entries
    instead of replacing previous entries.
-   Report tokenization errors with line information in the
    Esperanto-English importer.
-   Prevent em dashes from disrupting phonetic output alignment.
